CONTROLS -- every check above has to be shown able to come out the other way
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A checker that has never failed is a checker nobody has tested. Each control
below states what it is and which outcome counts as the control SUCCEEDING.

CONTROL 1 -- "the guard is what protects the server, not luck".
  Rebuilds both objects from copies whose guard has been weakened from
  `#if !defined( DEDICATED ) && defined( __EMSCRIPTEN__ )` to
  `#if defined( __EMSCRIPTEN__ )`, and relinks the server with them.
  THE CONTROL SUCCEEDS IF THESE DIFFER FROM BASE. If they matched, CHECK 4
  and CHECK 5 would be measuring nothing.
  [PASS] CONTROL 1: unguarded web/build-m0/render/rSysdep.o differs from base
         base       = 1022f9ec62b81304f47cca4366a13581
         unguarded  = f6516e659be1aaa54a3aa9c829f674db
  [PASS] CONTROL 1: unguarded web/build-m0/engine/eSound.o differs from base
         base       = aca51a511f51fdee88a45a64b3bee59b
         unguarded  = 249e88f5de38bbfa05fd16a8b62f4cb7
  [PASS] CONTROL 1b: an unguarded server links to a DIFFERENT wasm
         required  2488298 bytes  9718a2a64978cb6e9b95ea2f0454cca5
         unguarded 2488298 bytes  830a19dcd0687ad1a1f4101a457349f0
         size delta 0 bytes
         THE SIZE CHECK ALONE WOULD NOT HAVE CAUGHT THIS. Both values changed only
         in content, not in length: sr_maxFPS 360 -> 60 and buffer_shift 0 -> 1 are
         edits to the initialisers of two i32s that already exist in the data
         segment, so the segment is the same length and so is the module. This is
         why the invariant has to be quoted as "2,488,298 bytes AND md5 9718a2a6..."
         and why a size-only check would have passed a broken dedicated server.

CONTROL 2 -- A CONTROL THAT IS SUPPOSED TO PASS. Not filler: it is the only
